### Third-Party Data and Open-Source Acknowledgments

This software integrates data, mathematical models, and open-source libraries
from the following authoritative scientific and engineering sources:

1. **NASA Near-Earth Object Web Service (NeoWs)**: Near-Earth object orbital
   parameters, miss distances, and physical estimates provided by NASA / JPL
   under the NASA Open Innovation and Open Data Policy.
2. **NASA Planetary Defense Coordination Office & CNEOS / JPL SSD**: Fireball
   bolide reports and Sentry collision monitoring records courtesy of NASA JPL.
3. **CelesTrak**: Satellite two-line element sets (TLEs) provided courtesy of
   Dr. T.S. Kelso and CelesTrak.
4. **Three.js**: 3D WebGL rendering engine under MIT License (Copyright (c)
   2010-2026 Three.js authors).
5. **satellite.js**: SGP4/SDP4 satellite orbit propagation under MIT License
   (Copyright (c) Shashwat Kandadai).
6. **astronomy-engine**: Planetary position calculations under MIT License
   (Copyright (c) Don Cross).
7. **Leaflet**: Interactive cartographic display under BSD 2-Clause License
   (Copyright (c) Vladimir Agafonkin).

